# Deploy quick-card (stage + prod)

"Deploy" = **promote the branch AND rebuild the container on the box.** A
`git push` alone changes nothing live — the VMs do not auto-deploy. Full runbook:
[docs/deployment_runbook.md](mdc:docs/deployment_runbook.md). PowerShell: chain
with `;`, never `&&`.

## Identity / boxes (the part people get wrong)

You SSH **key-based** as **`dmadmin`** to both boxes (no password prompt from this
workstation). `dmadmin` is the only account that owns the Docker socket + the
`/home/dmadmin/docker-{staging,production}` trees. The old `qtip-admin` @
`/opt/qtip` (host-PM2) account is **retired** — never deploy there.

| What | stage | prod |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Host | `10.90.15.6` | `10.90.15.5` |
| Project dir | `/home/dmadmin/docker-staging/qtip-app` | `/home/dmadmin/docker-production/qtip-app` |
| `code/` tracks branch | `stage` | `production` |
| App container | `qtip-app-stage` | `qtip-app` |
| DB container | `qtip-db-stage` | `qtip-db` |
| URL | `https://qtip-stage.dm.local` | `https://qtip-prod.dm-us.com` |

Confirm identity before acting: `ssh dmadmin@10.90.15.6 'whoami; docker ps --format "{{.Names}}"'`.

**Credentials:** never hardcode the DB password. In-container commands reference
the container's own `$MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD` / `$MYSQL_DATABASE` env vars (see the
runbook). The literal lives in the operator secret store for break-glass only —
do not paste it into commits or this repo.

## 1. Promote (fast-forward only; never commit onto an env branch, never force-push one)

```powershell
# main -> stage
git checkout stage; git merge --ff-only main; git push origin stage; git checkout main
# stage -> production (only AFTER stage verifies)
git checkout production; git merge --ff-only stage; git push origin production; git checkout main
```

If `--ff-only` is rejected, the env branch has commits `main`/`stage` lacks —
reconcile on `main`, never force-push.

## 2. Deploy on the box (pull + rebuild)

```powershell
# STAGE
ssh dmadmin@10.90.15.6 'git -C /home/dmadmin/docker-staging/qtip-app/code pull --ff-only; cd /home/dmadmin/docker-staging/qtip-app; docker compose up -d --build'
# PROD (after stage verify)
ssh dmadmin@10.90.15.5 'git -C /home/dmadmin/docker-production/qtip-app/code pull --ff-only; cd /home/dmadmin/docker-production/qtip-app; docker compose up -d --build'
```

- **`.env`-only change** (no code): `docker compose up -d` (no `--build`).
- **DB migration in the release:** back up first, then apply BEFORE the rebuild.
  The runtime image often lacks the Prisma CLI, so **probe first** and expect to
  use the SQL fallback — full decision tree + PowerShell-safe commands in
  runbook §3.1–§3.3.
- **Build fails on ONE box only (same commit/lockfile)?** The build must stay
  hermetic — the repo `.dockerignore` keeps host `node_modules`/generated code out
  of the image context. A stale `code/<ws>/node_modules` on a box is the classic
  cause of "stage passed, prod failed". Never edit files on the box to fix it;
  root cause + one-line diagnosis in runbook §3.2a.

## 3. Verify

Browser: `https://qtip-stage.dm.local` / `https://qtip-prod.dm-us.com` (self-signed
cert prompt expected). Those names do NOT resolve from inside the box (curl over
SSH returns `000`); to check on the box, hit the published port
(`docker ps` for the mapping) or `docker exec <app> wget -qO- http://localhost:5000/health`
(the container has no `curl`). Confirm HEAD:
`ssh dmadmin@10.90.15.6 'git -C /home/dmadmin/docker-staging/qtip-app/code rev-parse HEAD'`.

> **Prod caveat:** re-confirm prod's container names + published port with the
> identity check on the first prod deploy of a cycle — stage is verified
> firsthand more often than prod.
